erms of  authentication the MacBook Pro actually  has touch ID right here in the corner of  the keyboard so you could easily log in  and make purchases whatever you want to  do using your fingerprint but  the Microsoft Surface laptop 3 actually  has Windows hello  right there  so you just open it up it looks at your  face recognizes it unlocks it now I  don't know how secure this is but it's  so much more convenient you don't even  have to put your finger anywhere just  unlocks automatically I really wish that  Apple would implement this into the  MacBook now looking at the overall  layout of these two laptops they look  very similar but there are definitely  some differences first of all you can  tell that you have speaker grilles right  here on the MacBook and they're  completely missing on the surface that's  actually because the speaker's are  underneath the keyboards so we're  definitely gonna have to test out those  speakers and see which ones are better  in just a minute and of course you can  see that the trackpad on the MacBook Pro  is quite a bit larger than the one on  the surface and this is actually not  that small a lot of other Windows  laptops have smaller track pads in this  so overall we're pretty happy with the  size of this trackpad but you definitely  can't beat the size of the one on the  macbook pro as for the keyboard I can  tell that the surface does have it  recessed a little bit deeper into the  laptop itself whereas this just goes  down a little bit and we have like these  rounded keys compared to this  traditional squared off keys and we can  see that the MacBook Pro actually has  the touch bar this year which is really  nice but some don't like it because they  prefer to have a physical Escape key but  I actually don't mind it it's not too  bad you've got all your options right  here and you can customize a lot of it  on this little display right here and  one big difference you can instantly  notice is the difference in the displays  n