t the surface got around  38% faster graphics score then on the  MacBook Pro so that's really impressive  so the performance you're getting here  on the surface is quite a bit better  than on the MacBook Pro and finally to  finish off performance I want to test  the disk speed test so I got aja right  here so let's test it on both of these  right here and once again the surface  actually beats out the MacBook Pro you  got a slightly higher read score and  almost double of the write scores and  that's something we usually don't see  because Mac books usually have faster  SSD speeds compared to Windows laptops  so once again Microsoft  job in the performance Department so  with all that said which laptop is the  better bye  of course if you prefer Mac you're  definitely going to go with the MacBook  Pro but if you could go either way  for $1,300 the surface does have more  performance it has more storage  so spec wise the surface actually beats  out the MacBook but when you look at the  fine details like the display quality  the color accuracy the trackpad other  stuff like that the MacBook Pro actually  might be better for professionals who  are trying to do photo editing video  editing or things like that especially  because of the Thunderbolt 3 ports the  lack of Thunderbolt 3 on the surface is  actually a really big downfall of this  laptop so if you're trying to use it  with an e GPU with a monitor with a  thunderbolt ii dock you actually won't  be able to do that on the surface but  other than that if you need a basic  really premium high quality laptop this  is actually a really good option because  the all aluminum build the keyboard the  trackpad the display everything is  actually really decent and very good for  a Windows laptop so of course if you  like Mac this is the way to go because  you still get really good performance  you have excellent display quality you  can use the Thunderbolt 3 with any GPU  monitors everything else so in reality  this is actually one of the toughest  choices of how to make but I'd say  because you get more storage on the  surface and you get such good  performance and everything else is just  so high-quality premium on the surface I  would definitely choose this one over  the MacBook Pro if you don't need  Thunderbolt 3 now if you do need  Thunderbolt 3 it's definitely gonna have  to be the MacBook Pro so I hope you guys  like this comparison definitely click  that circle above to subscribe and check  out some of those other videos right  there thanks for watching and we'll see  you in the next video  [Music]

